  "details": "Now that each user in the \"Online in Private Worlds\" section displays their icon instead of their banner/avatar image, it's much more difficult to identify users just from their icon, since everyone is already used to the images they would see before this update.\n\nFurthermore, even if icons must be used instead now for some reason, they're smaller as circles rather than squares, so they're also just harder to see and parse in general without inspecting more closely.\n\nPair this with every user just being a gray rectangle with white text, and determining which friends are online goes from a quick glance at a few images, to reading a paragraph of usernames, maybe even clicking each one to read friend notes or look at banner pictures to refresh your memory.\n\nI'd suggest either moving back to using the banner images from before, or switching to rounded squares for icons, or both, or just allowing users to change any of these options from the settings menu (or, to avoid settings bloat, you could just add a small button on the social tab that opens a small menu that allows users to swap between each option with radial buttons).",
